# Morfa server environment. Local development: copy to .env.local (never committed) and fill only what you use.
# Production: your deployment's secret manager. Unset values keep a feature off.

# The browser origin of the app, no trailing slash. Writes from any other Origin are refused. Required (https) in production;
# unset in development, where the app on 127.0.0.1/localhost ports 5400 (Vite) and 3400 (API) is allowed.
# APP_ORIGIN=https://app.morfa.example
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=3400
# Where uploaded pictures and thumbnails live (DATA_DIR/uploads).
DATA_DIR=data

# PostgreSQL 18 with three separate least-privilege roles (deploy/postgres/init-roles.sh creates morfa_migration,
# morfa_runtime and morfa_backup). No PG* variable is read. A loopback server may go without TLS; every other host
# requires sslmode=verify-full (MORFA_DATABASE_CA_CERT or MORFA_DATABASE_CA_CERT_FILE). Migrate with
# `MORFA_MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=… node --import tsx scripts/postgresql/migrate.ts --mode fresh`.
MORFA_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://morfa_runtime:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/morfa?sslmode=disable
# MORFA_MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://morfa_migration:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/morfa?sslmode=disable
# MORFA_BACKUP_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://morfa_backup:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/morfa?sslmode=disable
# Optional pool and timeout overrides: MORFA_DATABASE_POOL_MAX, MORFA_DATABASE_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS, … (server/postgresql/config.ts).

# Sign-in has no settings: a person types a name (docs/authentication.md). There are no passwords or outside providers, so a public
# deployment must sit on a private network or behind your own authenticating reverse proxy.

# The operators (server/admin/operators.ts): who opens the console (#admin, /api/admin/*: every account, payments, usage, and the
# support chat's answers below): account ids or addresses, comma separated. An account's address is its name in lower case at
# name.invalid (the name "Anna Petrova" is `anna petrova@name.invalid`; the console shows it): whoever types that name is the operator.
# Empty = nobody: to everyone else the console's routes answer 404, as an unknown route does.
MORFA_OPERATORS=

# Outgoing e-mail (server/mail.ts): the support chat's letters (below). Accounts have no mailbox, so nothing is ever sent to them.
# Unset = no letters. Any SMTP provider: smtps://user:password@host:465
# (or smtp://…:587 with STARTTLS). The sender must be an address the provider lets this account send from.
# MORFA_SMTP_URL=
# MORFA_MAIL_FROM=Morfa <team@example.invalid>

# The support chat (shared/support.ts): people write from the app ("Help ▸ Contact support", the file browser's
# button), the operators MORFA_OPERATORS names answer from the console (#admin/support). On whenever MORFA_OPERATORS names
# someone; SUPPORT_CHAT=0 switches the person's side off (the console keeps what was written). SUPPORT_NOTIFY_EMAIL (one
# address or several, comma separated) gets "New support request" when a person writes, at most once per conversation
# per 15 minutes; it needs the outgoing e-mail above. The person sees who answers as "Morfa team", never an operator's name;
# "Online" only while an operator has the console open, the usual reply time only when measured from real answers. An answer the person has not seen for 10 minutes is
# e-mailed to them by the worker (at most hourly per conversation), again only with the outgoing e-mail above.
# SUPPORT_CHAT=0
# SUPPORT_NOTIFY_EMAIL=support@example.invalid

# The design tool (docs/design-tool.md) is Morfa's product and always on: server/index.ts keeps the design code's own
# ENABLE_DESIGN_TOOL switch at 1. DESIGN_TOOL_ACCOUNTS (ids or emails, comma separated) is a staged rollout: empty means every
# account. DESIGN_DOCUMENT_CACHE_BYTES is how much parsed JSON autosave keeps in memory (0 turns the cache off).
DESIGN_TOOL_ACCOUNTS=
DESIGN_DOCUMENT_CACHE_BYTES=67108864
# Big files (docs/decisions/big-files.md): DESIGN_BIG_FILES=1 replaces the fixed 50 000-layer / 20 MB cap with the big-file caps and
# the editor's memory budget, and loads pages on demand; the collab service reads MORFA_BIG_FILES=1 for the same. Off until the GPU
# renderer meets C3/C11 (docs/TARGETS.md §9).
DESIGN_BIG_FILES=0
# Live co-editing across several API processes (PostgreSQL LISTEN/NOTIFY); unset = one process.
# DESIGN_LIVE_FANOUT=postgres
# Vector PDF (docs/design-tool.md §Export): printed by a sandboxed Chromium headless shell (IMPORT_CHROMIUM_PATH). 0 where
# that browser cannot run: the editor then saves "PDF (raster)" in the browser. DESIGN_PDF_RENDER_MS is the longest one
# print may take (60 s).
ENABLE_DESIGN_PDF_EXPORT=1
DESIGN_PDF_RENDER_MS=60000
# 32-byte hex key (64 hex characters) that encrypts the sellers' API keys of the marketplace connections; never put it in frontend env.
HOSTING_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
# "Marketplaces" Performance Loop (docs/marketplaces.md §Performance Loop): sellers connect Wildberries and Ozon by API key, publish
# cards from the canvas, see their numbers on the frames and run A/B tests. Off unless 1. The keys are encrypted with
# HOSTING_ENCRYPTION_KEY (connecting answers 503 without it); APP_ORIGIN must be the public address Ozon downloads pictures from.
ENABLE_MARKETPLACE_API=0
